// BT-3556 (ADR 0124 Section 8/B9): a `late` slot fixture for
// shape_version_test.bt — an unassigned `late` slot is not a key in the
// dictionary a `migrateFromVN:` hook sees, so the hook guards the read with
// `at:ifAbsent:` (no new hook contract — the same guard
// docs/beamtalk-language-features.md's "gaps are fine" rule already
// recommends for any possibly-absent key). `late` needs no live process to
// exercise via `Behaviour >> migrateShape:from:` (ADR 0123 §2's
// "REPL-testable" promise), so this stays an `Actor subclass:` only because
// `late` is rejected on a Value's `field:` (late Slots section) — no
// instance is ever spawned.

Actor subclass: ShapeVersionLateSlot
  shapeVersion: 2
  late state: proc :: String
  state: flag :: String = "unset"

  class migrateFromV1: old :: Dictionary -> Dictionary =>
    old at: #flag put: (old at: #proc ifAbsent: ["absent"])
